# Next.js app (sandbox)

You are editing a **Next.js App Router** project inside a [Docker Sandbox](https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/) microVM.

## Commands (workspace root)

```bash
npm run dev
npm run build    # run before finishing
npm run lint
```

Dev server is usually on port **3000** when paired with the `workshop-app-nextjs` kit.

## App Router

- Routes under `src/app/` — Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only for hooks and events.
- Shared layout in `src/app/layout.tsx`; colocate metadata in layouts or pages.
- Data and copy in `src/lib/` — avoid hardcoding lists in page components.
- UI: shadcn in `src/components/ui/`; Tailwind + CSS variables in `src/app/globals.css`.

Before unfamiliar APIs, read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` — Next.js 16+ may differ from older versions.

## sbx

```bash
sbx ls
sbx run --clone cursor . --name feature/x
sbx secret set -g anthropic
```

- Never commit API keys — host `.env.local` syncs into the workspace.
- Prefer **clone mode** for feature branches.

Docs: https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/
